    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0106" n="96" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg96"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/11–644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Representative to the French Provisional
                        Government</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-06T18:00:00+01:00">November 6, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:24 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>351. Bidault<anchor n="15" xml:id="d68-f1"/> showed me this afternoon very
                    confidentially a note from the Russian Ambassador here<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d68-f2"/> setting out that after conversations in regard to the
                    European Advisory Commission with our Government and the British, it had been
                    decided to issue the well-known invitation to Massigli. The Russian Ambassador
                    went on to say that his Government had come to the conclusion that France should
                    be invited to become a permanent member of the Commission and had so
                    communicated to our Government<anchor n="17" xml:id="d68-f3"/> and the British
                    but had not yet had a reply in the premises from us or the British.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d68-f1" n="15" xml:id="d68-f1-content">
                <p>Georges Bidault, French Foreign Minister from September 9, 1944.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d68-f2" n="16" xml:id="d68-f2-content">
                <p>Alexander Efremovich Bogomolov.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d68-f3" n="17" xml:id="d68-f3-content">
                <p>Presumably a reference to the Soviet memorandum of October 29, <ref
                        target="#pg80">p. 80</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
